    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0051" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.61331/113: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the First Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Salisbury</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-29T15:00:00-05:00">September 29, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>270. Your 589, September 28, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="73" xml:id="d70-f1"/> Universal
                    Leaf Tobacco Company. You are authorized, in accordance with the request of the
                    company, to make an approach to the Japanese Embassy in Peiping along the lines
                    of the Department’s 332, September 22, 8 p.m., to Tokyo, provided you and the
                    Ambassador feel that such an approach might serve some useful purpose.</p>
                <p>Inform Tokyo and Tsingtao of any action taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
